  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during your stay. You came in because of anemia and black stools, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:48:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My doctor called me after my blood test and said my hemoglobin dropped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s correct. Your hemoglobin was 10, which is down from your usual 14. You also had melena—black, tarry stools—which suggests a GI bleed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:51:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I didn’t know that was serious. I’ve been taking ibuprofen for my hip pain—600 mg every four hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely what caused the bleeding. Ibuprofen can irritate the stomach, especially when combined with warfarin, which you’re on for your atrial fibrillation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:54:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t realize they could interact. I just wanted the pain to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. You also became a bit hypotensive in the ER—your blood pressure dropped to 80/50. We gave you fluids and vitamin K to reverse the warfarin effect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:57:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I felt dizzy for a minute. I didn’t want a blood transfusion—can you guarantee the blood is clean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2187-11-10 22:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I appreciate your concern. The blood supply is very safe, but we respected your decision. Instead, we gave you prothrombin complex concentrate to help your clotting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2187-11-10 23:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Is my stomach still bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2187-11-10 23:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not seeing active bleeding now. Your hemoglobin has been stable. But we’ll do an endoscopy tomorrow to check your stomach lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2187-11-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did the endoscopy this morning. You have diffuse gastric ulceration, but no active bleeding. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2187-11-11 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s healing? Does that mean I’m okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2187-11-11 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can heal, yes—but only if you stop ibuprofen and take a strong antacid called pantoprazole twice a day for eight weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2187-11-11 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can do that. But what about my hip pain? It’s really bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2187-11-11 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We ordered an MRI. Your X-ray showed mild arthritis, but the pain might be nerve-related. We’re checking for lumbar stenosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI results are back. You have lumbar stenosis—nerves in your lower spine are being compressed, especially on the right side."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why my leg hurts when I walk? It feels like cramping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s called pseudoclaudication. Since you can’t take NSAIDs, we’re prescribing oxycodone for pain and acetaminophen to take regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will surgery help? I don’t want to be on pain meds forever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A laminectomy could help, but we’d need to optimize your heart condition first. You’ve been having short runs of ventricular tachycardia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard about that. They said I should get a defibrillator, but I’m not sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with your heart function at 30%, you’re at higher risk for sudden cardiac death. An ICD could save your life if your rhythm becomes unstable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, but I’m not afraid of dying. I’ve lived with a lot. I just don’t want to be shocked all the time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll document your decision. But please discuss it again with your cardiologist. It’s important."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. What about my warfarin? Am I back on it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve restarted warfarin. You’re also on aspirin, so we’re being cautious. No bridging with heparin since you declined that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just don’t want more bleeding. But I know I need it for my stroke risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2187-11-12 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The key is balance—protecting your brain without harming your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2187-11-12 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your eye doctor also saw you. You mentioned new floaters?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2187-11-12 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, a few. Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2187-11-12 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They found a trace vitreous hemorrhage in your left eye, but no tear or detachment. It should clear on its own. Follow up with your ophthalmologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2187-11-12 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the redness in my eyes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2187-11-12 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s bilateral conjunctivitis. We’re giving you bacitracin ointment twice a day for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re being discharged today. Your hemoglobin is stable, and your stomach is healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take pantoprazole twice daily for eight weeks. No ibuprofen or NSAIDs. Use acetaminophen and oxycodone for pain as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my heart meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your heart medications—warfarin, metoprolol, ramipril, spironolactone, and torsemide. Weigh yourself daily and call if you gain over three pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. And I’ll see my PCP for the back pain and cardiology for the ICD discussion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re also scheduled to see a spine surgeon. Take care, and call us if you have any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel a lot better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay safe, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—should I watch for black stools again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. If you see dark stools, dizziness, or feel weak, go to the ER. But with the pantoprazole, it should heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. The nurse will bring your discharge papers shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll follow everything you said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the best thing you can do. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2187-11-13 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
